@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Trade decision actionability — build 2239
+
+Baseline: v1.22.23/build2238, commit 9e9cca569e8c9fb80b1843db4ae8fb248cfcb971, tree 7ac87bb9ff9f0da6186e50dedd0c93b9bd7bc727. Public readiness and repository identity were read before editing. No live Trade discovery, synchronization, preference write or private-cache inspection was performed.
+
+## Confirmed findings
+
+The actual generated qualified fixture offers and direct Evaluate shared their recommendation, bilateral eligibility, Neutral Market evidence and full weekly impact under the same prepared publication. There is no demonstrated verdict-engine discrepancy. The original comparison normalized JSON week-key types before comparing HTTP and Python objects; that transport distinction is not a numerical defect.
+
+At 375×667 the first qualified fixture card put its preview button 1,298.39 pixels below the top, after twenty direct paragraphs; the card was 1,783.39 pixels tall. The authoritative policy rule was available but the primary summary used generic wording. Optional result rows also suppressed the existing zero-qualified main-limit diagnosis. An empty catalyst list still produced a “Why now” heading.
+
+## Narrow correction
+
+Read the recorded final verdict and existing reason vocabulary once for a concise decision lead shared by cards and Evaluate. Keep costs, explicit picks, the two-sided summary and full legal-lineup evidence. Move the existing preview action before longer summaries; preview still does not adopt or submit an offer. Preserve unknown counterparty motivation and evidence-specific next steps. Show the existing bounded-search diagnosis when displayed offers are optional rather than qualified. No enumeration, ranking or eligibility change.
+
+Timing presentation accepts only a supported bye/playoff catalyst whose generation, weeks and numerical change match the already admitted comparison. Retained timing is not revalidated. General roster alignment and unstructured text are not labeled urgency.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+Disposable retained-source fixtures, real authenticated HTTP and released JavaScript exercise a qualifying capital exchange, a 995/75 rejected marginal upgrade, meaningful current production, incomplete partner/reserve evidence, Neutral/Custom distinctions and actual one-QB K/DEF and Superflex legal slots. Both pre/post lineups remain independently optimized. Four viewports: 320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and 1280×900. Chromium is not physical iPhone/Safari acceptance.
+
+Original baseline probes, failed focused attempts and final logs must remain separate in task evidence. Full local canonical and required hosted gates must pass on the exact final tree before publication. The release evidence records actual results; this document does not predeclare them.
+
+Production live account acceptance requires an existing authorized session plus safe current resource admission. No credential workaround, repeated401attempt or forced heavy production workload is part of this correction. Missing live access is reported independently of fixture and public deployment verification.
